+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+"Open": no meeting notes record it as done.
+
+## 11 August: data stall and full disk
+
+**Impact:** Overnight, incoming data stopped for about 2.5 hours; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+
+**Cause:** One malformed data batch jammed processing. Endless retries filled the database disk with logs, halting writes.
+
+**Fix:** A restart that set the bad batch aside; disk clean-up.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80%: no owner; open. Disk hit 85% in September, spotted by hand.
+- Paging rules: Elif and Sunil; done. Pages now escalate after 15 minutes.
+- Stop bad batches jamming processing: Jonas; open.
+
+## 21 September: public API outage
+
+**Impact:** 47 minutes on a Monday morning; nearly all customers could not reach the public API.
+
+**Cause:** The API's security certificate expired. Its automatic renewal had been failing silently on an outdated access key.
+
+**Fix:** Certificate renewed, API restarted.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Renewal repaired, now alerts on failure: no owner; done.
+- Reminder 14 days before certificate expiry: no owner; open.
+- Alert on days left before expiry: no owner; open.
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist: no owner; open.
+- Log steps during incidents: whoever handles one; standing rule.
